Bash Accurately dump the little advice topic
IN
SP="C:/Users/faig3/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/d--Work-Morrowind-reborn/c16716bf-a0ad-4c7a-a0cb-12e526dc19a0/scratchpad"
awk '
function flush(){ if(rec=="INFO" && act!=""){ printf "  [%d] INFO=%s ACTOR=%s\n      RULE=%s\n      TEXT=%s\n", ++n, id, act, (rule==""?"(none)":rule), txt } }
/^Record: DIAL /{flush(); rec="DIAL"; dial=$0; sub(/^Record: DIAL "/,"",dial); sub(/"$/,"",dial); if(dial=="little advice"){show=1; n=0; print "===== TOPIC: " dial} else show=0; act=""; next}
/^Record: INFO /{flush(); rec="INFO"; id=$0; sub(/^Record: INFO "/,"",id); sub(/"$/,"",id); txt=""; act=""; rule=""; next}
show&&/^  Text: /{txt=substr($0,9)}
show&&/^  Actor: /{act=substr($0,11); gsub(/"/,"",act)}
show&&/^  Select Rule:/{rule=rule "; " substr($0,17)}
END{flush()}
' "$SP/info.txt" | head -40

OUT
===== TOPIC: little advice
  [1] INFO=305996678198439929 ACTOR=Vedam Dren
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=Don't make enemies. If someone is determined to be your enemy, then fight. But do not turn friends or potential friends into enemies through arrogance or carelessness.
  [2] INFO=19139287163203512660 ACTOR=caius cosades
      RULE=; lobal       Random100                        <  33
      TEXT=How do you judge a job's difficulty? Consider three things: location, opposition, and payoff. Long walks into the wilderness are usually tougher than local or town tasks. Tough opponents make tough jobs. Daedra, vampires, rogue Telvanni -- you'll learn which ones to look out for. And finally, if the reward offered is large, the dangers will be large, too.
  [3] INFO=190453052515814369 ACTOR=caius cosades
      RULE=; lobal       Random100                        <  66
      TEXT=How do you know when you've been given a task too tough for you? You have to decide. If it seems too tough, it probably is. Guild stewards and faction leaders don't really know how much you can handle. And some don't care. You have to look out for yourself. But as long as you haven't been given a deadline for completion, it's usually smart to wait and tackle those tough jobs after you're stronger and better equipped.
  [4] INFO=633623660273719775 ACTOR=caius cosades
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=About doing quests for factions. If you try to complete every task you're given, sooner or later you'll run into trouble. Don't assume that, just because someone gives you a job, you ought to be able to complete it. When you get a job that's over your head, be patient. Go do something else for a while, and come back when you're tougher, better skilled, and better equipped.
  [5] INFO=15147129031918618185 ACTOR=crassius curio
      RULE=; ournal      B6_CurioHort                     >= 50; ournal      B6_HlaaluHort                    <  50
      TEXT=I am sure you can persuade Dram Bero to support you as Hortator... if you can find him. Orvas Dren has Nevena Ules and Velanda Omani in his pocket. You might want to make a little trip to the Dren Plantation before talking to them. And then there's Yngling Half-Troll.
  [6] INFO=16369126751670624337 ACTOR=vodunius nuccius
      RULE=; unction     NPC Level                        <  2
      TEXT=New here? Take the silt strider to Vivec or Balmora. Fast and cheap. No trouble with wild animals. And smugglers. And bandits. And outlaws. Go see Darvame Hleran over at the strider port, over the bridge and east along the water. And tell her Vodunius Nuccius sent you.
  [7] INFO=6806119891911025550 ACTOR=vodunius nuccius
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=Take the silt strider to Vivec or Balmora. Fast and cheap. Go see Darvame Hleran over at the strider port, over the bridge and east along the water. And tell her Vodunius Nuccius sent you.
  [8] INFO=124735414790028426 ACTOR=eldafire
      RULE=; ead         Melar Baram                      == 0; ead         Tanisie Verethi                  == 0; ead         Mulvisie Othril                  == 0
      TEXT=You look like you can take care of yourself. Then why don't you do something about those smugglers in Addamasartus cave? It's right over there near the silt strider port. Yet these guards! Look at them. Just strutting around. Someone must have paid them to ignore the smuggling going on here.
  [9] INFO=1248319992938512979 ACTOR=arrille
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=If you want to live to a ripe old age, buy a weapon and as much armor as you can wear and still run from trouble. Buy a spell or two. And practice your skills. Don't practice on citizens. We call that foul murder, and we don't like it. But you can kill smugglers and bandits and other outlaws all you like. Outlaws have no rights. Plenty of adventurers make a living from killing and looting outlaws. That smuggler scum down in Addamasartus, for instance. The cave down near the silt strider platform.
  [10] INFO=16890297712091512590 ACTOR=arrille
      RULE=; unction     NPC Talked to Player             == 0
      TEXT=If you need directions, talk to our local scout, Elone the Redguard. She's here in the tradehouse somewhere. And you might want a copy of 'Guide to Vvardenfell' -- I think I still have a copy for sale.
  [11] INFO=31005160372891213503 ACTOR=trerayna dalen
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=Stay out of things that don't concern you, outlander. This affair is between myself and Therana. I want no help. I'll tolerate no interference.
  [12] INFO=1304524464103348091 ACTOR=estinan
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=Stay clear, outlander. Trerayna Dalen is our mistress, and this is a high Telvanni affair.
  [13] INFO=4709312971804825108 ACTOR=endring
      RULE=(none)
      TEXT=You don't belong here, outlander. Trerayna Dalen is our mistress, and this is a high Telvanni affair.
